{
  "id": "arousal-theory",
  "term": "arousal theory",
  "definition": "Arousal theory, as used here in optimal stimulation or arousal theory, holds that some people seek stimulation and show reduced fearfulness, which can lead to weaker responses to hostile or threatening facial expressions. In this context, it is used to explain why adolescents with conduct disorder may orient less to threatening emotional cues.",
